  "term": "chronic obstructive pulmonary disease",
  "definition": "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease is a progressive, varied lung condition marked by shortness of breath, chronic cough, sputum production, and often repeated lower respiratory tract infections. It can reduce exercise capacity and physical functioning.",
